xctest.py: Swift Testing's results as their tests, and a run of no tests a failure

A parameterized test's line ("Test f(n:) with 3 test cases passed") made a test named "f(n:) with 3 test cases", and
a failure's message took in every Swift Testing line after it (tests and test cases starting, the suite ending), which
went into the JUnit. The test is now f(n:), and Swift Testing's other lines end a failure's message (its "↳" lines,
the expectation's values, stay in it). A run in which no test ran (an -only-testing that matched nothing) said
"TEST SUCCEEDED" and exited 0; it now fails, with exit status 2.

